 value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those 75 years. In 2025, October to November finished at 41% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 52% and April to May at 58% on the middle. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, and grid 20905 bottomed out at 63% that year.</p>"}
